)\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Full-face photos\"}]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":\"Full-face photographs and any comparable images of a person.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Unique identifying features\"}]}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"Any other\"}],\" unique characteristic, code, or identifier that could be tied to a person.\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"6c:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"If health information contains any of the above identifiers (even initials or partial data), it is considered “identified” (and thus PHI). PHI is not just medical test results or diagnoses. It includes any personal detail linked to health data. For example, a lab result tagged only with a patient’s initials and birthdate is still PHI because those are identifying elements. Developers must assume that any combination of health info with personal identifiers is PHI and handle it with the highest care.\"}]\n6d:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"de-identifying-phi-safe-harbor-vs-expert-determination\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"De-Identifying PHI: Safe Harbor vs. Expert Determination\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#de-identifying-phi-safe-harbor-vs-expert-determination\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to De-Identifying PHI: Safe Harbor vs. Expert Determination\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"When building healthcare applications, you’ll often need to de-identify data for analytics, testing, or research purposes. HIPAA provides \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/for-professionals/special-topics/de-identification/index.html\",\"children\":\"two methods\"}],\" to transform PHI into non-PHI data that can be used more freely:\"]}]\n6f:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"safe-harbor-method-the-developer-friendly-checklist\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Safe Harbor Method: The Developer-Friendly Checklist\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#safe-harbor-method-the-developer-friendly-checklist\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Safe Harbor Method: The Developer-Friendly Checklist\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n70:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Safe Harbor is the “just remove these 18 things” approach. It’s prescriptive and straightforward to implement programmatically, making it perfect for most development scenarios.\"}]\n71:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"How it works: Remove all 18 HIPAA identifiers from your dataset. If nothing remains that could identify a person, the data is de-identified.\"}]\n73:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Pros: Easy to implement, verify, and audit. You can write a script that strips these fields.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Cons: Data loses specificity—no dates beyond year, limited geographic info, which may reduce analytical value.\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n74:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"expert-determination-the-data-science-approach\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Expert Determination: The Data Science Approach\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#expert-determination-the-data-science-approach\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Ex"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"pert Determination: The Data Science Approach\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n75:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Expert Determination uses statistical methods to ensure re-identification risk is “minimal” while preserving more data utility.\"}]\n76:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"How it works: A qualified expert applies techniques like:\"}]\n77:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Date shifting (offsetting all dates by a random number of days)\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Geographic aggregation (county instead of ZIP)\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Age bucketing (45-50 instead of exact age)\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"K-anonymity (ensuring each record matches at least K others)\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n79:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The expert certifies that combinations of these quasi-identifiers appear in multiple patients, preventing unique identification.\"}]\n7a:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Pros: Retains more analytical value—you can still see temporal patterns and geographic trends.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Cons: Requires statistical expertise, formal risk analysis, and documentation.\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n7b:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"practical-tips-for-developers\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Practical Tips for Developers\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#practical-tips-for-developers\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Practical Tips for Developers\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n7c:[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Default to Safe Harbor for test data, development environments, and basic analytics. It’s foolproof if implemented correctly.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Watch out for free text. A note saying “45-year-old engineer at Tesla” contains identifiers. Free text fields need special handling or exclusion.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Consider Limited Datasets as a middle ground. These retain some identifiers (like dates) but remove direct identifiers (names, contacts). They’re still PHI but useful for research under data use agreements.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Automate where possible. Build de-identification into your data pipelines:\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"5. Remember: De-identification isn’t just deletion. A 103-year-old with a rare disease on a specific date is still identifiable even without a name. Think about combinations of data points.\",[\"$\",\"br\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"br\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"When in doubt, strip it out.\"}],\" It’s better to have less detailed, fully de-identified data than to accidentally leak PHI through an obscure combination of quasi-identifiers.\"]}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"best-practices-for-handling-phi-in-development\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Best Practices for Handling PHI in Development\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#best-practices-for-handling-phi-in-development\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Best Practices for Handling PHI in Development"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Consider these non-negotiable requirements, not optional guidelines.\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"encryption-and-storage\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Encryption \u0026 Storage\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#encryption-and-storage\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Encryption \u0026 Storage\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n82:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Always encrypt PHI at rest and in transit\"}],\". Use AES-256 for data at rest and TLS 1.2+ for all network communications. Never store encryption keys in source code—use a dedicated key management service like AWS KMS or HashiCorp Vault. \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.com/docs/security/hipaa\",\"children\":\"Neon does this for you\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Never use real PHI in dev/test environments\"}],\". Use synthetic or properly de-identified data for development and testing. If production data is necessary for debugging, require formal approval, use it in an isolated environment, and wipe it immediately after use.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Secure all backups and archives\"}],\". Encrypt database dumps and backup files before storage, and treat them with the same security controls as production data. When decommissioning storage devices that contain PHI, use secure wiping tools or physical destruction methods.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n83:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"access-control-and-authentication\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Access Control \u0026 Authentication\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#access-control-and-authentication\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Access Control \u0026 Authentication\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n84:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Enforce unique user IDs and strong authentication\"}],\". Never allow shared accounts for PHI access—every user needs a unique, auditable identity. Implement multi-factor authentication (MFA) for all systems handling PHI, especially patient portals and admin interfaces.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Implement role-based access control (RBAC) with the principle of least privilege\"}],\". Users should only access the minimum PHI necessary for their job function. A lab technician entering results doesn’t need access to complete patient histories, and a billing clerk doesn’t require clinical notes. \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.com/docs/security/hipaa\",\"children\":\"Neon does this for you\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Set aggressive session timeouts\"}],\". PHI applicati"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ons should automatically log out users after short periods of inactivity. Use secure session management with HttpOnly and Secure flags on cookies, and never expose session IDs in URLs.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"api-and-integration-security\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"API \u0026 Integration Security\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#api-and-integration-security\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to API \u0026 Integration Security\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Never put PHI in URLs or query parameters\"}],\". URLs end up in server logs, browser history, and monitoring tools—use POST requests with PHI in the request body instead. Always use opaque identifiers (UUIDs) rather than revealing patient names or record numbers in API paths.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Require authentication for all PHI endpoints\"}],\". No public API endpoints should ever return PHI—use OAuth 2.0, API keys with specific scopes, or signed tokens. Validate authorization on the server side for every request; never trust client-side checks alone.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Vet all third-party integrations for HIPAA compliance\"}],\". Any external service that touches PHI needs a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) and proven security controls. (e.g., \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.com/docs/security/hipaa\",\"children\":\"Neon has a BAA to conform with HIPAA compliance\"}],\"). This includes seemingly innocuous services such as email providers, SMS gateways, error tracking, and analytics tools.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n87:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"logging-and-monitoring\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Logging \u0026 Monitoring\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#logging-and-monitoring\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Logging \u0026 Monitoring\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Log all PHI access but not PHI content\"}],\". Record who accessed what record and when, but avoid logging the actual medical data—log “User X viewed Patient #123” not “User X viewed John Doe’s HIV results.” Treat audit logs as sensitive data with restricted access and long retention periods (six years or more).\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Actively monitor for suspicious patterns\"}],\". Set up alerts for unusual access patterns, such as bulk record downloads, after-hours access, or employees viewing records outside their department. Many insider breaches involve snooping on family members or celebrities—your monitoring should catch this.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Never send PHI to external logging services\"}],\". Avoid accidentally exposing PHI through error logs, debug output, or monitoring tools. If you must log errors involving PHI, mask or hash sensitiv"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"e values before they reach any third-party service.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Neon uses \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://www.pgaudit.org/\",\"children\":\"PGAudit\"}],\" for \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.com/blog/postgres-logging-vs-pgaudit\",\"children\":\"extensive, HIPAA-compliant audit logging\"}],\".\"]}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"development-practices\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Development Practices\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#development-practices\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Development Practices\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Implement de-identification early in your pipeline\"}],\". Build Safe Harbor de-identification into your data export tools—it’s easier to strip the 18 identifiers programmatically than to handle PHI everywhere. For test data generation, use this de-identified production data or fully synthetic datasets.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Sanitize all free text fields\"}],\". Clinical notes and comments often contain hidden identifiers like “45-year-old Tesla engineer” that violate de-identification. Either exclude free text from de-identified datasets or use NLP tools to detect and redact identifying information.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Plan for incident response from day one\"}],\". Build features to quickly revoke API keys, deactivate user accounts, and generate compliance reports. You should be able to answer “who accessed what and when” within minutes, not hours, when investigating a potential breach.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"common-pitfalls-to-avoid\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Common Pitfalls to Avoid\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#common-pitfalls-to-avoid\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Common Pitfalls to Avoid\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$61:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Watch out for metadata leaks\"}],\". Patient photos contain PHI in EXIF data, file names might include patient names, and browser caching can expose sensitive data on shared computers. Set Cache-Control: no-store headers and sanitize all file metad